// window/x11/bind/xcms.cst — Xcms.h: colour as a measurement.
//
// Xcms is X's device-independent colour system: CIE XYZ, u*v*L, Lab, Luv, and
// the conversion machinery between them and whatever the monitor actually does.
// It exists so that a colour specified once looks the same on two different
// screens, which is a real problem and one this layer does not attempt.
//
// Nothing in window/x11/ calls any of it. The software path packs
// 0xAARRGGBB into a TrueColor visual and the server writes those bits to the
// framebuffer; there is no colour management anywhere in that sentence, and
// pretending otherwise would be worse than not doing it.
//
// It is bound because ../../window.md asks for every function libX11 exposes,
// and because 69 functions is a real part of what a program driving X11 itself
// might reach for. If colour management ever becomes this library's business it
// belongs in a colour layer above, not here.

